      "id": "context-2024",
      "title": "Three gauges, one published day",
      "narration": "The U.S. Geological Survey reports daily mean discharge at three distinct Potomac gauges. On 2024-10-01, the published values were 5,580 ft³/s at Hancock, 23,600 ft³/s at Point of Rocks, and 17,300 ft³/s at Little Falls. The three points mark stable station IDs, not equal drainage areas.\n\nThe photograph shows the river area at Whites Ferry as context. It is not a picture of a gauge measurement or of this day.",
