    {
      "id": "limits",
      "title": "What the snapshots can tell us",
      "narration": "These are USGS Approved daily mean discharge records for station-local dates in Eastern time. The records have no additional qualifier, but approval does not make the three catchments interchangeable. Hancock and Point of Rocks have documented regulation or hydroelectric influences; Little Falls has documented diversions and reservoir effects. Different drainage areas and travel time also limit a direct upstream-to-downstream reading.\n\nThe two dates support a descriptive station-by-station comparison. They do not measure reach gain or loss, isolate a cause, describe unregulated flow, establish a trend, or assess flood risk.",
      "content": {
        "semantics": "The meaning and limits of two published station-day summaries.",
        "attribute": "daily_mean_discharge in ft^3/s",
        "relationship": "Return to the same locations while interpreting the comparison."
      },
